
C-FOCAL,1969

01.10 T "PROGRAM FOR DETERMINING FRAME RATE OR SCALE SPEED FOR"!
01.11 T "MINIATURES USED IN MOTION PICTURE SPECIAL EFFECTS."!!
01.20 T "IS THIS FILM TO BE SHOWN AT NORMAL SOUND SPEED? IF"!
01.21 A "YES, PLEASE TYPE '1'; IF NO, PLEASE TYPE '2'." Z
01.22 I  (Z-2)2.1,2.2,1.3
01.30 T "SORRY, BUT YOUR CHOICE IS LIMITED TO '1' OR '2' -- PLEASE"!
01.31 T "ANSWER PROPERLY"!;G 1.2

02.10 S R=24;G 3.1
02.20 A "AT HOW MANY FRAMES PER SECOND WILL THIS FILM BE SHOWN?" R
02.21 G 3.1

03.10 T "WHAT IS THE SCALE OF THE MODEL?  THAT IS, PLEASE STATE HOW"!
03.11 T "MANY INCHES OF LINEAR MEASURE ON THE MODEL WOULD EQUAL ONE"!
03.12 A  "FOOT ON A FULL-SIZED OBJECT" S
03.20 S S=S/12
03.30 T "IS THE MODEL GOING TO BE INFLUENCED BY GRAVITY? THAT IS, IF"!
03.31 T "THE MODEL IS GOING TO FALL OR ROLL BECAUSE OF THE ACTION OF"!
03.32 A "GRAVITY, PLEASE TYPE '1'; OTHERWISE TYPE '2'"G
03.40 I (G-2)3.5,5.1,3.41
03.41 T "SORRY, BUT YOU MUST ANSWER WITH A '1' OR '2'"!;G 3.3
03.50 T "IF GRAVITY IS TO PLAY A PART, THE SCALING FACTOR MUST BE"!
03.51 T "YOUR SCALE IS " S*12, " INCHES PER FOOT, YOU WILL HAVE"!
03.52 T "TO SHOOT AT A RATE OF " R*(1/FSQT(S)), " FRAMES PER SEC-"!
03.53 T "OND TO ACHIEVE A MATHEMATICALLY PERFECT SIMULATION OF THE"!
03.54 T "FULL SCALE EVENT"; Q

05.10 T "IF GRAVITY IS NOT A CONSIDERATION, THE APPARENT"!
05.11 T "MOTION OF A MINIATURE OBJECT DEPENDS DIRECTLY UPON ITS"!
05.12 T "SCALE AND MAY BE SHOT AT " R," FRAMES PER SECOND"!
05.13 T "WITHOUT PENALTY.  IT IS ASSUMED THAT THE SPEEDS WE ARE"!
05.14 T "CONSIDERING ARE IN MILES PER HOUR.  HOW FAST (IN MPH)"!
05.15 A "WOULD THE OBJECT BE GOING IF IT WERE FULL SCALE?"V
05.16 T "FOR AN APPARENT VELOCITY OF " V, " MILES PER HOUR,"!
05.17 T "THE MODEL WOULD HAVE  TO BE TRAVELING AT "!
05.18 T S*V*88/60, " FEET PER SECOND"!!!; Q
*}